  "body": "### Summary\nUnder CLOB Fill Rounding of the documentation: \n> \"On CLOB fill, filled amounts are rounded down to the nearest lot. FOK fill orders _should_ not revert if only the amount rounded off is left unfilled\"\n\nHowever, it is the case that FOK fill orders **will revert** even if only the amount rounded off is left unfilled.\n\n### Details\nThe `currMatch.matchedAmount` is a multiple of lot size as it is derived from\n```solidity\nmatchData.baseDelta = (matchedBase.min(takerOrder.amount) / lotSize) * lotSize;\nmatchData.quoteDelta = ds.getQuoteTokenAmount(matchedPrice, matchData.baseDelta);\nmatchData.matchedAmount = matchData.baseDelta;\n```\n\nIf the incoming order has amount that is not a multiple of lot size, the line `incomingOrder.amount -= currMatch.matchedAmount;` will return a non-zero amount and therefore revert with `FOKOrderNotFilled()`.\n\n`if (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();`\n\nTherefore, the FOK order is reverted even though only the amount rounded off is left unfilled.\n\n### Remediation\nRound the incoming order down to the nearest lot size",
  "proof_of_concept": "### PoC\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {Side, Order} from \"../../contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"../../contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        address maker = users[0];\n        address taker = users[1];\n        vm.label(maker, \"maker\");\n        vm.label(taker, \"taker\");\n\n        uint256 amountInBase = 1 ether;\n        uint256 price = 100 ether;\n\n        // Change Lot Size to 10\n        vm.prank(address(clobManager));\n        clob.setLotSizeInBase(10);\n        \n        // Maker looking to sell\n        setupOrder(Side.SELL, maker, amountInBase, price);\n    \n        // Fill order does not have any checks\n        uint256 takerAmount = amountInBase - 5; // not a multiple of lotSize\n        setupTokens(Side.BUY, taker, takerAmount, price, true);\n\n        ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs memory fillArgs = ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs({\n            amount: takerAmount,\n            priceLimit: price ,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            amountIsBase: true,\n            fillOrderType: ICLOB.FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL\n        });\n\n        vm.expectRevert(\"FOKOrderNotFilled()\");\n        vm.prank(taker);\n        clob.postFillOrder(taker, fillArgs);\n    }\n}\n```",
